## sakura-crossing

    Upstream    https://github.com/kenton-gmi/sakura-crossing
    Commit      de01898e89c7f6ab3fad93fa802f0f5ac66fbd81
    Licence     MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Kenton Wang
    Vendored at src/maps/city/vendored/
    Files       59 JavaScript source files, byte identical to upstream
    Licence text travels with them at src/maps/city/vendored/LICENSE

The 59 files are exactly the transitive import closure of the three entry
points the freestyle city map uses: `src/world/index.js` (57 files),
`src/core/post.js` and `src/core/sky.js`. Neither `src/core/audio.js`,
`src/core/player.js`, `src/core/hud.js`, `src/main.js` nor `src/world/ebike.js`
is on that path, so no upstream music, walker, interface or entry point is
incorporated, and the 3.9 MB music mp3 in the upstream repository is not
vendored.

## sakura-crossing, kiln cel kit

    Upstream    https://github.com/kenton-gmi/sakura-crossing
    Licence     MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Kenton Wang
    Copied at   src/maps/bando/cel/
    Files       toon.js, post.js, util.js, plus LICENSE

Copied so Industrial bando can use the same toon materials and ink pipeline without
fetching anything under src/maps/city (check 16). The copies import this
map's palette.js instead of the city's. toon.js also exports
releaseMaterials(), which clears the material caches on dispose. Licence
text travels with them at src/maps/bando/cel/LICENSE.

Three of the 59 city files carry changes; the other 56 are byte identical
to upstream.

  * `world/index.js` carries the four line change recorded in full at
    `src/maps/city/vendored/PATCH-world-index.diff`, which makes the planet
    bake optional so the city can be taken in its flat authoring. The change
    adds a parameter with the upstream behaviour as its default, so calling
    `buildWorld(scene)` still does exactly what it does upstream. It also
    carries the town thinning pass of 2026-08-26, which is a set of edits to
    the town's own composition rather than to its interface: dressing removed,
    planting thinned. Those are described in PROGRESS.md rather than in a diff
    file, because a diff against upstream would be the wrong record for a
    change to what the town contains.
  * `core/toon.js` carries the one line change recorded at
    `src/maps/city/vendored/PATCH-core-toon.diff`, which drops `flatShading`.
  * `world/petals.js` carries the three line change recorded at
    `src/maps/city/vendored/PATCH-world-petals.diff`, which gives its
    instanced meshes the names `petalField` and `fallenPetal`. Every other
    instanced set in the town is named (`sakuraCanopy0`, `groveCanopy1`,
    `hillTuft`, `lakeReed`); these three were the exception, and two passes
    of ours read mesh names to decide what a drawn thing means. Nothing about
    what is drawn changes.

The line above used to read "fifty eight of the 59 city files are byte
identical", which stopped being true when `core/toon.js` was patched and was
never corrected.

Everywhere else our shell needs different behaviour from a vendored class, it
subclasses or wraps it in our own GPLv3 code under `src/maps/city/` rather
than editing the vendored copy, so an upstream update is a re-copy plus one
patch rather than a merge.

